  "id": "ALAS2-2026-3988",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2 2017.12 - ALAS2-2026-3988: medium priority package update for fence-agents",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-12 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-12 16:30:00"
  },
  "severity": "medium",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-59939:\n\thttplib2 is a comprehensive HTTP client library for Python. Prior to 0.32.0, httplib2 performs unbounded decompression of HTTP response bodies encoded with Content-Encoding: gzip or deflate in _decompressContent in httplib2/init.py, allowing a malicious or compromised HTTP server to return a small compressed payload that expands to an arbitrarily large size in memory and causes MemoryError or OOM-kill in the client process. This issue is fixed in version 0.32.0.\n",
